; std/sample: statistics, and all of it free.
;
; The mean of 2, 4 and 9 is 5; 1 in 3 is 33 percent; 7 sits halfway through the
; range 5 to 9. Three quantities computed, none of them fired, and all three
; written into the single prompt the program pays for.
;
; The sample is written at the mediator, which takes as many branches as you
; give it — so no macro here had to know how many there were, and none of them
; is arity-locked.
; expect: calls 1
; expect: clean
; expect: contains 5 33 1/2
; expect: answers
((# std/sample)
 ($ "Reply with exactly the three values below, separated by single spaces, and nothing else.\n"
    |(std-mean ([sum] 2 4 9) ([count] 2 4 9))| " "
    |(std-percent 1 3)| " "
    |(std-scaled 7 5 9)|))
